            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>According to folklore, the kikimora was once a swamp or forest spirit that came to prefer living in a peasant's home to dwelling out in the muck and cold. They look rather like the people they live alongside but sometimes have animalistic features.</p><hr /><p>House spirits are a collection of fey who live among peasants and poor rural folk. They hide themselves from mortal eyes—hence why they're so commonly called \"spirits\"—but their presence is always felt. Given suitable respect, these house fey take a decidedly parental interest in the mortals they live with, doing all manner of work around the household. They cook, they clean, they sweep, they chop wood, they care for animals, they tend the stove. If disrespected, however, they becomes a veritable plague of ill will.</p>",
